# Promotions

You can now create promotions to lower the price of a membership. The discount is a link to the registration form, printed as a QR code.

From the Other (…) menu, open [Promotions](/promotions). Nothing extra to turn on. Once the promotion is created, copy its QR code onto a flyer, a poster, a coupon, or a gift card. The person who opens it sees a banner with the discount amount. Once they register, the fixed amount comes off one membership. There is nothing to type. The amount appears on the membership and on the invoice, on its own line.

A promotion can be used once (a gift voucher) or by several people over a given period. A [price reduction](/handbook/price_reductions) remains a different case, one a member can choose when registering.

More detail in [the handbook](/handbook/promotions).
